<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang={RetroHexChatWeb.I18n.html_lang()} dir={RetroHexChatWeb.I18n.html_dir()}>
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <.head_meta />
    <%!-- Two ways to title a page live here, and the difference matters.

          `page_title` is the framework's: LiveView re-sends it on every change
          and its client writes `document.title`. Connect and the dev dashboard
          use it.

          The chat cannot: its tab title also carries the activity flash, so a
          single client-side owner (DocumentTitleHook) composes the two. It
          renders its first-paint title as `initial_title` instead, which
          LiveView does not track — and with no `default` here, LiveView's
          mount-time `putTitle` returns without writing, leaving the hook alone
          with `document.title`. Adding a default would hand the mount write
          back to the framework and clobber the hook. --%>
    <.live_title>
      {assigns[:page_title] || assigns[:initial_title]}
    </.live_title>
    <meta name="robots" content={RetroHexChatWeb.SEO.noindex_content()} />
    <.app_icons />
    <.head_assets />
    <link phx-track-static rel="stylesheet" href={~p"/assets/css/retrohex.css"} />
    <script phx-track-static type="module" src={~p"/assets/js/app.js"}>
    </script>
    <script phx-track-static type="module" src={~p"/assets/js/faro_entry.js"}>
    </script>
  </head>
  <body class="bg-background font-system text-text">
    {@inner_content}
  </body>
</html>
